<title>CANADA: Canada sells no gold in April.</title>
<headline>Canada sells no gold in April.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada sold no gold in April, the Finance Department said on Monday.</p>
<p>Its holdings remained at 3.1 million ounces as of April 30, the department said.</p>
<p>The Canadian government has a policy of gradually selling off its gold reserves and replacing them with interest-bearing assets.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
